HTTP Verbs (methods) 

 

Guideline: 

 

Developers may implement the following HTTP Verbs, as applicable to the resource: 

GET - returns the current value of a resource 

PUT - completely replaces the value of a resource 

PATCH - partial updates to the value of a resource 

POST - creates a new resource, or invokes an action (RPC style) 

DELETE - deletes a resource 

TRACE - SHOULD only be used in non-production environments for debugging / testing purposes. In addition, the TRACE response MUST be static, blank, or hardcoded, and MUST NOT reflect any element(s) of the request message.  

OPTIONS -. allows a client to determine the options and/or requirements associated with a resource, or the capabilities of a server. SHOULD only be enabled for CORS. 

  

HTTP methods SHOULD be used in compliance with their definitions under the HTTP/1.1 standard.  

The action taken on the representation will be contextual to the media type being worked on and its current state.  

 

