Versioning 

 

Updated Guideline combining the svb : Additional Topics-FCB API Guidelines v1.0.pptx 

 

Guidelines: 

 

APIs MUST support versioning. Always version the API from day one, even if you are not planning to support multiple versions.  

Without versioning, there are higher chances of consumers failing when a new version is released. 

APIs MUST be versioned using major versions as per FCB standards.  

For example: v1 

APIs SHOULD be versioned at the API service level, not for each API resource.  

For example: https://wwwcie.fcb.com/api/v1/users. 

MUST specify the version number in the URL in conformance with the FCB Standards.  

URL 

Pros 

Enhanced usability as the version is contained in the URL. 

Cons 

Provides an unstable resource URL that is not RESTful. 

Complicates implementation of HATEOAS because all URL links need to include the version number. 

For example: https://wwwcie.fcb.com/api/v1/users 

APIs MUST increment their version number for any breaking API change.   

New versions SHOULD NOT be created for adding fields and other non-breaking changes. 

Examples of non-breaking changes: 

Adding a method to an API interface 

Adding an HTTP binding to a method 

Adding a field to a request message 

Adding a field to a response message 

Adding a value to an enumeration 

Examples of breaking changes: 

Removing or renaming a service, interface, field, method, or enumeration value 

Changing the type of a field 

Changing a resource name 

Changing the URL of a resource  

 

 

